  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Fishing Ports and International Fish Markets - Phase 2 Preparation Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Integrated Fishing Ports and International Fish Markets Phase 2 Project, for board consideration in 2025 for $190 million, will modernize fishing ports to make MMAF quota-based policy operational. The ensuing project will be aligned with the following impact: contribution of the fisheries industry to the national economy increased. It will have the following outcome: profitability and environmental sustainability of the fishing industry improved. The ensuing project will have the following outputs: (i) climate-resilient and environmentally sustainable fishing port infrastructure constructed, and (ii) port management and fishery value chain services modernized.</narrative>
  </description>
